Extension-initiated requests must not advertise a chrome-extension:// Origin.

Sites that validate the Origin request header for CSRF (e.g. www.3gbizhi.com)
answer 403 the moment an extension request carries
"Origin: chrome-extension://<id>". Extension requests bypass CORS entirely,
so the header buys nothing and only breaks those sites.

Two layers are patched:

1. Blink's ResourceRequestHead::SetHTTPOrigin() drops the header for
   chrome-extension origins (extension pages, service worker, offscreen
   document).
2. The network service would synthesize the header straight back from
   request_initiator in CorsURLLoader::MaybeSetOriginHeader(); drop it there
   too when the initiator scheme is chrome-extension, including the
   headers_update_params bookkeeping.

Generated for Chromium 155.0.8059.91.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/loader/fetch/resource_request.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/loader/fetch/resource_request.cc
index 1397eee..fc54f9e 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/loader/fetch/resource_request.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/platform/loader/fetch/resource_request.cc
@@ -329,6 +329,15 @@ void ResourceRequestHead::SetHttpHeaderField(const AtomicString& name,
 }
 
 void ResourceRequestHead::SetHTTPOrigin(const SecurityOrigin* origin) {
+  // OHOS: requests made by an extension (its pages, service worker and
+  // offscreen document) do not advertise "chrome-extension://..." as their
+  // Origin. Sites that validate Origin for CSRF reject that value outright,
+  // and extension requests bypass CORS anyway, so leaving the header out is
+  // both safe and what the sites expect.
+  if (origin->Protocol() == "chrome-extension") {
+    http_header_fields_.Remove(http_names::kOrigin);
+    return;
+  }
   SetHttpHeaderField(http_names::kOrigin, origin->ToAtomicString());
 }
 

